// Failure golden: a `Path` endpoint applying a name that is not in scope is
// REFUSED rather than quietly accepted.
//
// This is the sharpest form of the silent-acceptance defect the compound
// endpoint work closed. `nosuch` is defined nowhere in the program. When an
// application endpoint fell outside the type-position fragment the whole type
// degraded to the gradual unknown, so the definition below was admitted with
// no diagnostic at all -- a program mentioning a function that does not exist,
// accepted. The endpoint now reaches the core as the term it was written as,
// so the name is looked up and the identity is checked.
//
// (Pathological tree: testing artifact, not pedagogy -- ADR-52 Decision C.)

def refuted(x: Integer) -> F Path(Integer, nosuch(x), x) {
  ret here(x)
}

//@ expect-diagnostic: type mismatch
